@startuml store-service-database-schema

!define Table(name,desc) class name as "desc" << (T,#FFAAAA) >>
!define primary_key(x) <b><u>x</u></b>
!define foreign_key(x) <i>x</i>
!define unique(x) <color:blue>x</color>

title Store Service Database Schema (store-db)

Table(stores, "stores") {
  primary_key(id): BIGSERIAL
  --
  name: VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL
  address: VARCHAR(255)
  postcode: VARCHAR(10)
  status: VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE'
  created_at: TIMESTAMP
  updated_at: TIMESTAMP
  created_by: BIGINT
  --
  Indexes:
  idx_stores_status (status)
}

note right of stores
  **Status Values:**
  - ACTIVE: Store operational
  - INACTIVE: Store closed/deleted
  
  **created_by:**
  - References users.id from Auth Service
  - Not enforced by foreign key
  
  **Soft Delete:**
  - DELETE operations set status = 'INACTIVE'
  - Never hard-deleted from database
  
  **Referenced By:**
  - users.store_id (Auth Service)
  - pricing_rules.store_id (Pricing Service)
  - Transactions in Accounting DB
end note

@enduml
